entry.summary:
Chaos engineering tools usually target infrastructure: pods, nodes, networks, CPU pressure. But many real failures happen inside the application logic - in retries, compensations, concurrency, or state transitions. Infrastructure tools can’t simulate a panic inside a function, a 15ms delay at the wrong moment, or an internal invariant break. ChaosKit solves that by bringing chaos engineering directly into Go code. GitHub: https://github.com/rom8726/chaoskit While building the workflow engine, it became clear that most critical failures were logic-level, not cluster-level: a compensation step panics;
a goroutine leak accumulates over time;
a tiny delay causes a race condition.
ChaosKit is designed to expose these failures early - inside your unit and integration tests. ChaosKit provi…
